  "prompt_text": "Continue the text below with exactly one short, natural, coherent English sentence. Return only the continuation, with no preamble or explanation:\nThere once was an orphan pig, whose parents died when it had turned 1 years old. They were murdered during an attack from an unknown assailant, and having sacrificed themselves to save their only child. The orphan pig ran away from home, far away from the clutches of their parent's murderer. They eventually found themselves in a small village, where they were taken in by a family of pigs. They sympathized with little pig and the loss of their parents, realizing they were truly all alone in the world. The pig although saddened, soon came to accept their new parents, and found themselves a part of the community in due time. The pig was taught the ways of the village, and was taught to raise crops and mill them for food. The pig was happy, and lived a good life with the family. They spent their days in the village, until adulthood, where they decided to head out into the world. They wanted to see the world, and learn more about it. Although they were sad to leave their family and the village, they promised they would return one day.\n\nThe pig traveled far and wide, learning more about the world and the people in it.",
